    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #296\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-109-module-contract-02-12-register-module-thr_8fqycp9yfj`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #109, building on #108's merged `ModuleManifest`/`ModuleRegistry` foundation (merged `develop` into this branch first to pick it up):\n\n- **`packages/module-registry`**: `heartbeatRuleKinds` upgraded from bare strings to `{kind, schemaExport, nextFireAtExport}` descriptors, matching the epic's original spec; added `reservedTaskNames`/`reservedHeartbeatRuleKinds` options so a module colliding with a core task name or rule kind fails to load loudly; added `getTaskDefinitions()`/`getHeartbeatRuleKindDefinitions()` to resolve a module's declared tasks/rule kinds to their actual imported schema/handler functions.\n- **`packages/data`**: heartbeat rule parsing and next-fire computation now validate/dispatch against the union of core rule kinds and an injected `HeartbeatRuleKindRegistry`, resolved fresh from `ModuleRegistry` on every sweep/fire invocation — a heartbeat whose module got deactivated is skipped (with `last_error` recorded) rather than dispatched. Added `mergeModuleTaskList` to compose the queue's `TaskList` from core handlers plus active modules' task definitions, validating each payload against its module schema before invoking the handler.\n\nAll 365 tests across the monorepo pass, and every package typechecks cleanly with `tsc --noEmit`.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
