    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #296\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nWorking tree was already clean (no uncommitted changes), and the commit addressing the code review findings has been pushed to the same branch: `bb/relay-109-module-contract-02-12-register-module-thr_8fqycp9yfj`.\n\n## Summary\n\nPushed the fix for PR #296's code review findings:\n- **High**: `recomputeAllForTimezoneChange` now catches a deactivated module's rule kind per-row (mirroring `sweepDueHeartbeats`'s existing pattern), instead of letting one bad row abort the whole batch/transaction.\n- **Medium**: `mergeModuleTaskList` now re-checks each module task name against `CORE_TASK_NAME_SET` as a defense-in-depth guard, so a module task can't silently shadow a core handler even if the caller built its `ModuleRegistry` without `reservedTaskNames`.\n- **Low (test coverage)**: added integration tests for `recomputeAllForTimezoneChange` with both an active and a deactivated module rule kind, plus a unit test for the new core-name collision guard in `mergeModuleTaskList`.\n\nFull monorepo typecheck is clean and all 368 tests pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
