    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #296\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-109-module-contract-02-12-register-module-thr_8fqycp9yfj`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe remote branch had picked up a `develop`-merge commit since my last push, so I merged that in locally (clean, no conflicts — it only touched unrelated IMAP flag-typing files from PR #295) before pushing my new commit.\n\nPushed change addresses the remaining open finding from the code review on PR #296:\n- **Medium**: `createHeartbeatFireTask`'s `getHeartbeat` call now catches the case where a heartbeat's module rule kind was deactivated between the sweep enqueuing the job and the fire job actually running. It records the failure via `recordHeartbeatFailure` and skips firing, instead of throwing uncaught (which would retry up to `max_attempts` and dead-letter the job with no `last_error` ever recorded). A new integration test exercises this race directly.\n\nFull monorepo typecheck is clean and all 371 tests pass (up from 369 due to tests picked up from the merged `develop` changes).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
