    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #296\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-109-module-contract-02-12-register-module-thr_8fqycp9yfj`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe remote branch had again picked up a `develop`-merge commit (bringing in unrelated inbox-pipeline validation changes from PR #297), so I merged it locally — clean, no conflicts — before pushing.\n\nPushed change addresses both remaining findings from the code review on PR #296:\n- **Medium**: `ModuleRegistry.loadModule` now validates that a `heartbeatRuleKind`'s `schemaExport` is structurally schema-shaped (has a `safeParse` method), rejecting a malformed export loudly at load time instead of failing confusingly later inside `parseHeartbeatRule`.\n- **Medium**: `setHeartbeatEnabled(id, false)` and `updateHeartbeatRule` no longer require the heartbeat's *current* rule to still parse — a heartbeat stuck on a deactivated module's rule kind can now be disabled or repointed at a working rule (re-enabling still correctly requires a resolvable calculator, since it computes `next_fire_at`).\n\nFull monorepo typecheck is clean and all 377 tests pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
